B f2-063 WRONG {'text': 'To find the frequency of light given its wavelength, we use the wave equation:\n\n$$\nc = \\lambda \\nu\n$$\n\nWhere:\n- $ c $ is the speed of light in a vacuum, approximately $ 3.00 \\times 10^8 \\, \\text{m/s} $\n- $ \\lambda $ is the wavelength\n- $ \\nu $ is the frequency\n\nWe are given:\n- $ \\lambda = 500 \\, \\text{nm} = 500 \\times 10^{-9} \\, \\text{m} $\n\nRearranging the equation to solve for frequency:\n\n$$\n\\nu = \\frac{c}{\\lambda}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\nu = \\frac{3.00 \\times 10^8 \\, \\text{m/s}}{500 \\times 10^{-9} \\, \\text{m}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\nu = \\frac{3.00 \\times 10^8}{5.00 \\times 10^{-7}} \\, \\text{Hz}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\nu = 6.00 \\times 10^{14} \\, \\text{Hz}\n$$\n\nNow convert to terahertz (THz), where $ 1 \\, \\text{THz} = 10^{12} \\, \\text{Hz} $:\n\n$$\n\\nu = \\frac{6.00 \\times 10^{14} \\, \\text{Hz}}{10^{12} \\, \\text{Hz/THz}} = 600 \\, \\text{THz}\n$$\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n**600 THz**'}
